 ## Overview
-Gaussian Avatars is a method for reconstructing photorealistic, animatable head avatars by anchoring 3D Gaussians to a parametric FLAME mesh [S1][S3, unofficial]. It solves the challenge of maintaining topological consistency and rigging capabilities in dynamic head reconstruction by constraining each Gaussian to its corresponding mesh triangle [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike methods that predict Gaussian parameters via MLPs conditioned on pose [S1][S3, unofficial], Gaussian Avatars optimizes Gaussians directly while enforcing geometric constraints, enabling high-fidelity rendering and relighting [S2, unofficial].
+Gaussian Avatars is a method for reconstructing photorealistic, animatable head avatars by anchoring 3D Gaussians to a parametric FLAME mesh [S1][S3, unofficial]. It associates each FLAME mesh triangle with a Gaussian that is optimized for the scene while being constrained to remain within its corresponding triangle [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike methods that predict Gaussian parameters via feedforward networks conditioned on pose [S1], Gaussian Avatars optimizes the Gaussian ellipsoid parameters directly while enforcing geometric constraints, enabling high-fidelity rendering and relighting [S2, unofficial].
 
